# November 23, 2026: a first scatter of places across the parts of Idaho the Atlas had nothing in: the Bear Lake and
# Cache valleys of the southeast, Pocatello, Rexburg, the Lemhi and Yankee Fork country, the Magic Valley, the Camas
# Prairie and the Palouse, Weiser and Sandpoint. State drawn as the one with the fewest places (tools/choose.py --thinnest).
# Sources read in this session: Wikipedia articles (tools/wiki_raw.py), National Register nomination forms (NPGallery
# "_text" PDFs, read with tools/page.py), the Idaho State Historical Society's site pages, the National Park Service,
# the Forest Service's Custer page, the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints' Paris Tabernacle page, the Latah
# County Historical Society, the Historical Museum at St. Gertrude, the Oneida Stake Academy Foundation, the Idaho
# Heritage Trust, SAH Archipedia and the Ensign Peak Foundation. No interior was seen by any source unless the entry says so.
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
